  "id": "incidental-learning",
  "term": "incidental learning",
  "definition": "Incidental learning is learning that happens as a byproduct of doing a task rather than from being directly told to learn a particular strategy or shortcut. In the source context, people discovered an unmentioned shortcut through practice and then decided whether to use it.",
